\ rgb3: RGB LED, common cathode: red on PB10, green on PB11, blue on PB12  ok.
\ Paste all of it into the console, or put it in a file after wiring.fs.  ok.
  ok.
\ PB10 (pin 30) → 270 Ω → red LED → GND  ok.
$48000400 constant rgb3-red-port  \ GPIOB  ok.
10 constant rgb3-red-pin  ok.
\ PB11 (pin 33) → 56 Ω → green LED → GND  ok.
$48000400 constant rgb3-green-port  \ GPIOB  ok.
11 constant rgb3-green-pin  ok.
\ PB12 (pin 34) → 56 Ω → blue LED → GND  ok.
$48000400 constant rgb3-blue-port  \ GPIOB  ok.
12 constant rgb3-blue-pin  ok.
  ok.
\ ms: wait n milliseconds, counted by SysTick at 16 MHz  ok.
\ (lib_systick uses SysTick too: with it loaded, use its delay-ms)  ok.
: ms ( n -- ) Redefine ms.  ok.
  15999 $E000E014 !  0 $E000E018 !  5 $E000E010 ! \ SysTick: wrap every 16000 cycles  ok.
  0 ?do begin $E000E010 @ $10000 and until loop   \ count the wraps  ok.
  0 $E000E010 ! ;                                 \ SysTick off again  ok.
  ok.
: rgb3-colour ( red green blue -- )               \ each: 0 = off, else on  ok.
  0<> if 1 rgb3-blue-pin lshift else 1 rgb3-blue-pin lshift 16 lshift then \ BSRR: blue on or off  ok.
  rgb3-blue-port $18 + !  ok.
  0<> if 1 rgb3-green-pin lshift else 1 rgb3-green-pin lshift 16 lshift then \ BSRR: green on or off  ok.
  rgb3-green-port $18 + !  ok.
  0<> if 1 rgb3-red-pin lshift else 1 rgb3-red-pin lshift 16 lshift then \ BSRR: red on or off  ok.
  rgb3-red-port $18 + ! ;  ok.
: rgb3-off ( -- ) 0 0 0 rgb3-colour ;  ok.
: rgb3-init ( -- )  ok.
  1 1 lshift $4002104C bis!                       \ RCC AHB2ENR: clock for GPIOB  ok.
  %11 rgb3-red-pin 2* lshift rgb3-red-port bic!   \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %01 rgb3-red-pin 2* lshift rgb3-red-port bis!   \ MODER: 01 = output  ok.
  %11 rgb3-green-pin 2* lshift rgb3-green-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %01 rgb3-green-pin 2* lshift rgb3-green-port bis! \ MODER: 01 = output  ok.
  %11 rgb3-blue-pin 2* lshift rgb3-blue-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %01 rgb3-blue-pin 2* lshift rgb3-blue-port bis! \ MODER: 01 = output  ok.
  rgb3-off ;  ok.
  ok.
\ Red, green, blue in turn until a key is pressed  ok.
: rgb3-cycle ( -- )  ok.
  rgb3-init  ok.
  begin  ok.
    1 0 0 rgb3-colour 300 ms  0 1 0 rgb3-colour 300 ms  0 0 1 rgb3-colour 300 ms  ok.
  key? until rgb3-off ;  ok.
  ok.
\ Try it: rgb3-init 1 1 0 rgb3-colour (yellow)   or   rgb3-cycle (Enter stops it)  ok.
  ok.
rgb-init 100 40 0 rgb-colour  ok.

[chip] TIM1 CH1 is enabled, but MOE in TIM1_BDTR is 0: an advanced timer keeps its outputs off until MOE is set
